  partName: Exhaust Manifold Bolt (4)
  description: The Exhaust Manifold Bolt (4) is a tiny, complex-shaped fastener located
    at the top-center-rear of the engine, made from Material.001. It plays a crucial
    role in securing the exhaust manifold to the engine, ensuring a tight seal and
    preventing leaks. One interesting aspect of this bolt is its ability to withstand
    high thermal stresses, as it is exposed to the hot exhaust gases, and its complex
    shape allows for even distribution of clamping force.
